{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Afterward the children of Israel shall return.</b> For they are the children of Judah and Israel who were exiled first, therefore he included them all. And the sense of <b>and David their king</b> — this is the Messiah, as in <i>and David My servant shall be their prince forever</i> (Ezekiel 37:25)." "<b>And shall fear YHWH</b> — that they shall return swiftly when the end comes, to their land in haste, suddenly, in the manner of <i>they shall tremble like a bird from Egypt</i> (Hosea 11:11), where it is written <i>and I will settle them on their homes, declares YHWH</i>. And the faithful witness to this interpretation is that he said <i>in the latter days</i>, and these are the end of the prophecy of the prophets, as in <i>and it shall be in the latter days, the mountain of the house of YHWH shall be established</i> (Isaiah 2:2), and there it is written <i>and they shall beat their swords into plowshares</i> (Isaiah 2:4), and all these are for the future."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:50:02.059089877Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}